{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/17573-using-radio-sickness-holy-engineers-in-demon","id":17573,"title":"Using Radio Sickness/Holy Engineers in Demon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-25T00:10:14-08:00","id":17573,"title":"Using Radio Sickness/Holy Engineers in Demon","content":"<i>Danse Macabre</i> gives us the phenomenon known as Radio Sickness, in which the God-Machine blasts the afflicted with strange electronic phenomena that forms an answer to a not-yet-asked question. The 'disease' intensifies (ultimately resulting in aggravated damage if not fixed) until the victim realizes what question they have been given the answer to. They then broadcast the signal, and the sickness ends until they are given another answer.<br /> <br /> It's written for vampires and focuses on the specific information written up in the original Marco Singhe blurb (I still think that the &quot;government conspiracy to hold the remains of the angel that gave the world death&quot; thing is a little silly), but I feel like it could easily be re-purposed for either Demon or a GMC Mortals game.<br /> <br /> How, then, would you make use of &quot;time paradox God-Machine Jeopardy prophecy disease?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T09:53:37-08:00","id":17769,"title":"","content":"Well, in keeping with the Techgnostic Espionage theme, I've been thinking it could be really cool to have a Demon (probably an Inquisitor or a Saboteur) hacking into a certain frequency and listening in on the Angels/God-Machine's communique, like a fugitive listening in on police radio, to anticipate their movements and either avoid them or strike when/where it hurts. Radio Sickness would be a really cool way to model this mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T09:57:06-08:00","id":17770,"title":"","content":"I'd say the radio sickness was inflicted not from a great distance but from a local transmitter, which is some kind of Infrastructure - maybe it uses the vampires as stopgaps when other infrastructure has been short-circuited, or maybe all the Holy Engineers in the area have ultimately been enabling one or several G-M projects. So then I can seed encounters with the weird and dangerous Holy Engineers over a few stories, and then because of player followup or happy coincidence, they can discover the transmitter. They can tap into it, destroy it - or start directing the vampires towards their own goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}